Description: mass spectrometry data viewer, processing and analysis tool
 mMassX is an open source, multiplatform application for the analysis
 and processing of mass spectrometry data. It is a maintained fork of
 mMass, a mass spectrometry tool originally by Martin Strohalm that
 was widely used in proteomics but whose development had stalled.
 .
 Features include:
  - viewing and annotating mass spectra from common raw/exported
    formats (mzXML, mzData, mzML, MGF and plain text)
  - peak picking, deisotoping and de-noising
  - mass calibration and mass defect plotting
  - peptide/protein mass fingerprinting and fragment ion search
  - a compound editor and periodic table for elemental composition
    searches
 .
 This package reintroduces mass spectrometry tooling that was
 previously packaged as mmass and removed from Debian in 2019 after
 upstream development had ceased; mMassX is its actively developed
 successor.
